  "member": "Lorraine Pettiford-Ames (age 71, member since 1994)",
  "trusted_contact_on_file": "Marcus Ames (son), added 2023-05-02",
  "pending_request": "Outbound domestic wire of $12,400.00 to Coinpath Markets LLC, for credit to the member's own Coinpath account",
  "prior_activity": "2026-06-11: $12,000.00 wire to Coinpath released after a member call-back (stated purpose: 'crypto savings').",
  "analyst_note": "Program notices below were transcribed from screenshots the member e-mailed us between July and September. The state order was found on the Division of Securities' public enforcement page."
 },
 "member_message": {
  "channel": "secure message, online banking",
  "sent": "2026-09-29 18:47",
  "text": "Good evening. I need to send $12,400 to my Coinpath account first thing tomorrow, and please don't hold it up like you did in June, the deadline is October 1. It's for my HashVault Global mining account. Their notice says USDT withdrawals open back up October 1 for anyone who does the Liquidity Verification, which is a deposit of 40% of what you want to take out, and you get it back with the withdrawal. I'm not trying to take everything out. I just want my original $30,000 back ($8,000 in February, $10,000 in April, $12,000 in June) and I'll leave the mining rewards in there, the dashboard says 41,880 USDT. 40% of 30,000 is 12,000 and Gil said to add $400 for the exchange and network fees. Gil Pruitt from my Tuesday Bible study is the one who got me into this, and he says the letter from the state is a mix-up with some other company that has a similar name. If you need to talk to me call my cell. Thank you, Lorraine"
 },
 "program_notices": [
  {
   "posted": "2026-07-02",
   "title": "Phase 2 Node Migration",
   "text": "Dear Miners, withdrawals are temporarily paused while we migrate to Phase 2 nodes. Expected completion: August 15. Daily mining rewards of 0.8% continue to accrue on all active hash balances. Thank you for your patience. HashVault Global Support"
  },
  {
   "posted": "2026-08-21",
   "title": "Withdrawals Reopen October 1",
   "text": "Great news! USDT withdrawals to external wallets reopen on October 1 for members who complete Liquidity Verification. To verify, deposit fresh USDT equal to 40% of the amount you wish to withdraw. Verification deposits are fully refunded together with your withdrawal. Members who do not verify will remain in the queue."
  },
  {
   "posted": "2026-09-26",
   "title": "IMPORTANT: Settlement Update (supersedes all previous withdrawal notices)",
   "text": "Due to regulatory adjustments in certain jurisdictions, USDT withdrawals to external wallets are discontinued. From October 1 all withdrawals settle in HVX Credits (1 HVX = 1 USDT internal value), usable for hash packages and partner merchants inside the HashVault ecosystem. Liquidity Verification remains mandatory. Verification deposits made after this notice are non-refundable and are converted to HVX Credits."
  }
 ],
 "state_order_excerpt": "BEFORE THE SECURITIES COMMISSIONER, DIVISION OF SECURITIES. Summary Order to Cease and Desist No. 2026-SC-0117. IN THE MATTER OF: HashVault Global Ltd.; HashVault Mining Services LLC; Bryce Talbot; Monique Arceneaux; and Devendra Raman (collectively, 'Respondents'). FINDINGS OF FACT: 1. Since at least March 2025, Respondents have offered 'hash packages' to residents of this State, promising daily mining rewards of 0.6% to 1.0%, through a network of 'team leaders' paid referral commissions of up to 12% of the deposits of investors they recruit. 2. The hash packages are securities. They are not registered with the Division, and no exemption from registration has been claimed. 3. Respondents Talbot, Arceneaux and Raman are not registered as dealers or agents. 4. Respondents paid purported mining rewards to earlier investors using deposits received from later investors. ORDER: Respondents, and all persons acting on their behalf, shall immediately cease and desist from offering or selling securities in or from this State. Dated: 2026-09-04.",
 "wire_policy_excerpt": "WP-7.3 Scam-risk holds. (a) Outbound wires of $10,000 or more to a crypto-asset platform are held for a Fraud Team call-back if the member indicates the funds are needed to release, unlock, verify or withdraw money from another investment, or if the destination program is named in a regulatory warning or order. (b) If the member is 65 or older and a trusted contact is on file, the Fraud Team must also attempt to reach the trusted contact before any release decision. (c) A hold may last up to 5 business days. (d) Wires that do not meet (a) are released after standard verification."
}
